{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CrCxZhRFJVfKbDNRrQ9aP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go packages), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets, scaffolded). Human writes PRDs; orchestrator generates code.\n\n**Current State**: `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, and `pkg/format` (R1, R3) exist with tests in the source tree. No `cmd/` utilities exist on the working branch. Specs are complete for wc, cat, sponge, du. Specs are pending for rel02.0+ trivial utilities.\n\n**Current Release**: rel00.0 is largely satisfied by existing pkg/ code. rel01.0 (wc) is the earliest release with a spec-complete utility awaiting implementation. Dependencies (pkg/testutils, pkg/sys) are met.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nrel00.0's pkg/ packages exist in source code (trusting source over stale code_status). The next impactful work is rel01.0-uc001-wc — the first utility implementation, with spec complete and all dependencies satisfied. Implementation and tests must be split per planning rules; this task covers implementation only.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/wc implementation -- rel01.0-uc001-wc flag parsing, counting, and output formatting\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.0-uc001-wc.yaml (use case -- read first to find the PRD reference and execution flow)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (locate and read the wc PRD referenced by the use case above, matching prd*-wc.yaml)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.0.yaml (differential test cases that the implementation must satisfy)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component structure, design decisions DD2 and DD6)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests pattern -- understand how differential tests invoke the binary)\n      - pkg/sys/signal.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler for SIGPIPE handling)\n      - pkg/sys/terminal.go (IsTerminal if output detection is needed)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/wc/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"wc utility implementation -- flag parsing, counting logic, file handling, output formatting\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement all flags and default behavior specified in the wc PRD -- at minimum -l (lines), -w (words), -c (bytes), -m (chars), and the default mode that prints lines, words, and bytes when no flags are given\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement counting logic per the wc PRD -- line counting (newline-delimited), word counting (whitespace-delimited per C isspace), byte counting (raw bytes), and character counting (rune-based for multibyte input)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement file argument handling per the wc PRD -- read stdin when no file arguments are given, process multiple files sequentially, print a totals line when more than one file is provided, and treat the argument '-' as stdin\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement output formatting per the wc PRD -- right-aligned numeric columns with field widths matching GNU wc behavior, filename printed after counts, exit code 0 on success, exit code 1 when any file cannot be opened or read\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Create cmd/wc/ package with main.go per ARCHITECTURE.yaml cmd/ component structure -- one package per utility compiling to a standalone binary\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main() so the process exits silently on broken pipe, matching GNU behavior (prd002-sys R1.5)\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Target LC_ALL=C behavior only per ARCHITECTURE design decision DD6 -- use byte-oriented whitespace detection, no locale-aware character classification\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/wc/main.go exists and 'go build ./cmd/wc/' compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Running the binary with each of -l, -w, -c, -m individually produces output for only the requested count\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Running the binary with no flags produces line, word, and byte counts in that column order\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Running the binary with no file arguments reads from stdin until EOF and prints counts\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Running the binary with two or more file arguments prints per-file lines followed by a totals line labeled 'total'\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/wc/ passes with no diagnostics\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34609,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34609},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3099e531-d413-42e4-8db9-8a4d16e1c401","uuid":"5d1978df-c526-4150-b55a-803493273b9a"}
